---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---

<SiteLayout
	title="About"
	description="About Tomorrow-ish, a clearly labeled satirical newspaper reporting tomorrow's headlines today."
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<header class="page-header">
		<p class="section-kicker">About the paper</p>
		<h1>Close enough to tomorrow.</h1>
	</header>

	<article class="prose-page">
		<p class="prose-page__standfirst">
			Tomorrow-ish reports the next day's absurdities before they have the chance to deny everything.
		</p>
		<p>
			We are an independent satirical publication that follows today’s habits one questionable step into the future.
			Every headline and article on this site is fictional, and every public page says so plainly.
		</p>
		<h2>The premise</h2>
		<p>
			The news already contains the beginnings of its own absurd conclusions. Tomorrow-ish takes those beginnings
			seriously, extrapolates them irresponsibly, and publishes the result as tomorrow’s news today.
		</p>
		<h2>The standard</h2>
		<p>
			The aim is dry, intelligent satire presented with the care of a small newspaper: attentive writing, deliberate
			editorial judgment, and a clear line between invented stories and factual reporting.
		</p>
		<h2>The important part</h2>
		<p>
			Tomorrow-ish is satire. Do not rely on its stories as factual reporting. Source and context links, when present,
			identify background material; they do not make the fictional article itself true.
		</p>
	</article>
</SiteLayout>
